  "overview": "**Decathlon Vitamin** is a light-first design system anchored on `#fff` canvas surfaces with `#0b0b0c` primary ink (19.7:1 contrast) and `#0082c3` brand accent.\n\nTypography centers cleanly on `Roboto` (96px display down to 16px body), unified by `8px` base corner radius and stepped `#fff` -> `#eff1f3` surface layering.\n\nMaintained by **Decathlon**. Source: published token package (https://github.com/Decathlon/vitamin-web/tree/main/packages/sources/css/src/design-tokens), repo https://github.com/Decathlon/vitamin-web, package `@vtmn/css-design-tokens`, frameworks: css, react, vue, svelte. Inventory: **42** colors, **15** typography steps, and **8** documented components (Apache-2.0 license).\n\n### Layout & Spacing\n- **Grid & Control Spacing**: Derived from 8 component tokens with documented paddings: `10px 18px`, `9px 13px`, `18px 20px`, `4px 10px`, `10px 16px`.\n- **Hierarchy**: Group controls cleanly within `#eff1f3` cards; separate sibling sections using `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines rather than oversized whitespace.\n\n### Elevation & Depth\n- **Surface & Stroke Elevation**: Relies on crisp tonal contrast (`#fff` -> `#eff1f3`) and `1px solid color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines instead of heavy drop shadows.\n- **Interactive Lift**: Reserve higher surface brightness or focus outlines anchored on `#0082c3` for keyboard focus and active selection states.",
  "dos": "### Do\n- Anchor base views on `#fff` (light) with `#0b0b0c` primary text and `#0b0b0c` secondary labels.\n- Use `#0082c3` with `#f7f7f8` text (3.9:1) for primary CTAs, active tabs, and focus outlines.\n- Pair `Roboto` headings with `Roboto` body copy using documented weights and scale steps.\n- Apply `8px` base geometry across inputs and buttons (12px on outer containers).\n- Separate containers via `#eff1f3` surface shifts and `color-mix(in srgb, #0b0b0c 14%, transparent)` hairlines cleanly.\n\n### Don't\n- Do not invert the base canvas out of light polarity without explicitly switching component text tokens.\n- Do not place low-contrast muted ink or raw white text on light accents without verifying >= 4.5:1 WCAG AA contrast.\n- Do not invent arbitrary brand colors, unverified fonts, or synthetic heavy shadows outside the palette above.\n- Do not mix conflicting corner radii that clash with the system's `8px` baseline.\n- Do not truncate or drop border contrast on `input-default` fields and secondary buttons."
